class.description:
[CameraSettingsServer] is the settings domain [code]"camera"[/code]: it stores the field of view, whether it is vertical or horizontal, the near and far clip plane, and the game-side motion values (camera shake, head bob, motion blur) for the player. The settings resource is a [CameraSettings]; the file is [code]user://settings/camera.ini[/code] by default, in the format of [member ProjectSettings.settings/storage/format].
[b]Which cameras:[/b] every [Camera3D] in the group [code]"camera_settings"[/code] ([method get_camera_group]) gets the values when it enters the scene tree, also after a scene change, and every later change at once. Cameras can also be passed to [method add_camera]. Cameras outside the group, such as cutscene cameras, are never changed, also when they are current. In the editor, the cameras of the edited scene are not changed.
[b]Authored values:[/b] the first time a camera gets the settings, its own [member Camera3D.fov], [member Camera3D.keep_aspect], [member Camera3D.near] and [member Camera3D.far] are remembered. [method remove_camera] and [member CameraSettings.enabled] = [code]false[/code] give them back.
The defaults are the project settings [member ProjectSettings.settings/camera/field_of_view], [member ProjectSettings.settings/camera/keep_aspect], [member ProjectSettings.settings/camera/near] and [member ProjectSettings.settings/camera/far]. The domain is applied in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_PHASE_SCENE], before the main scene is loaded. Values out of range are clamped with a warning.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _ready():
	var camera_settings = Engine.get_singleton("CameraSettingsServer")
	$Menu/FieldOfView.value = camera_settings.get_field_of_view()
	# The player camera of every level gets the values.
	$Player/Camera3D.add_to_group(CameraSettingsServer.get_camera_group())

func _on_field_of_view_value_changed(value):
	Engine.get_singleton("CameraSettingsServer").set_field_of_view(value)

func shake(strength):
	var intensity = Engine.get_singleton("CameraSettingsServer").get_shake_intensity()
	$ShakeEffect.start(strength * intensity)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public override void _Ready()
{
    GetNode<HSlider>("Menu/FieldOfView").Value = CameraSettingsServer.GetFieldOfView();
    // The player camera of every level gets the values.
    GetNode<Camera3D>("Player/Camera3D").AddToGroup(CameraSettingsServer.GetCameraGroup());
}

private void OnFieldOfViewValueChanged(double value)
{
    CameraSettingsServer.SetFieldOfView((float)value);
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] This class does not exist when the engine is built with [code]disable_3d=yes[/code].
